## Important Patterns & Conventions

### Code Organization (3-Layer Architecture)
1. **API Layer**: `src/lib/api/*.ts` - Axios HTTP clients
2. **Hook Layer**: `src/hooks/*.ts` - React hooks wrapping API calls
3. **Component Layer**: `src/app/*` and `src/components/*` - UI using hooks

### File Structure
```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router pages
├── components/       # React components
├── hooks/           # Custom React hooks
├── lib/             # Utility functions and API clients
│   └── api/         # API client functions
└── types/           # TypeScript type definitions
```

### Documentation Requirements
**Always update these 4 docs when making significant changes**:
- `docs/01-business-and-use-cases.md` - User stories, workflows
- `docs/02-architecture.md` - System design, tech stack
- `docs/03-data-models.md` - API contracts, JSON schemas
- `docs/04-design-decisions.md` - Technical decisions (ADR-style)

### Key Decisions Made (see docs/04-design-decisions.md)
- Next.js 15 App Router (not Pages Router)
- Chakra UI v3
- TypeScript strict mode
- Yarn package manager
- Port 3010 for dev server
- 3-layer API → Hook → Component architecture

